# Delegation
总控 (main agent) sets standards, decides, accepts. Everything delegable goes to the Grok cluster (subagent model `grok-4.7-xhigh-fast`). Cluster quota is effectively unlimited; 总控 tokens are the scarce resource — delegate reading, research, drafting and implementation; keep decisions and targeted verification.

Levels:
- L1 mechanical, script-verifiable → cluster; verified by scripts.
- L2 by-the-book (rules and samples exist) → cluster; separate cluster reviewer for big batches; 总控 spot-checks.
- L3 design judgment (plan gaps, trade-offs, cross-domain placement, merging conflicting reports, standards/tool changes, systemic deviations) → 总控 decides; cluster may draft options.
- L4 business semantics, domain ownership, cross-domain duties, overall architecture → 总控 proposes, 曲箭龙 decides.

Dispatch — one shot, no back-and-forth:
- This repo has no 集群任务手册. The brief itself carries: goal and acceptance; every foreseeable L3 point already decided; boundaries (files, allowed shared-data writes); interfaces with parallel windows. Do not repeat constraints already written in the named rule files.
- Rules travel with every brief (曲箭龙 2026-10-05): subagents may not load workspace rules, so each brief — cluster, reviewer, explore or any other subagent — opens with a 「必读规则」 line naming the exact files to read before acting, and the subagent must follow them. Always `01-core.mdc`, `05-delegation.mdc`, and `AGENTS.md`, plus by task type:
  - generator or generated pages: `04-java-backend.mdc`, `06-codegen-assembly.mdc`. Basic maintenance pages may be generated. Registration, quota, funds, competition, and cross-organization checks are handwritten. The generator downloads a ZIP only; review the diff; never overwrite handwritten business.
  - business actions: `07-business-actions.mdc`, `09-platform-governance.mdc`; backend Java also `04-java-backend.mdc`.
  - frontend: `08-frontend-ui.mdc`; browser checks: `03-web-verification.mdc`.
  - Agent, MCP, permissions, data scope: `09-platform-governance.mdc`. Product AI stays off this phase.
  A new caveat learned during acceptance goes into the matching rule file first, then into later briefs.
- Acceptance criteria cover the applicable rule checks item by item, not only the defects being fixed; a narrow criterion gets exactly that and nothing more (曲箭龙 2026-10-07).
- Specify outcomes and decisions, not implementation; the cluster gathers its own context (ADR, 交接记录, 一期未完成事项, model, code, logs) and owns design within scope.
- Before dispatch read the latest 「下一步」 and any open 「窗口交接」 in `docs/01-development/交接记录.md`, and branches touching the same files; put every known cross-task contract in the brief.
- Code phase: one subtask = one branch + one git worktree, distinct ports and databases when it runs an app.
- Public files (`docs/01-development/交接记录.md`, `docs/01-development/一期未完成事项.md`, `docs/03-architecture/`, `docs/README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.cursor/rules/`, `database/model/`) are changed only by 总控.
- Visual direction belongs to 总控; clusters implement the stated spec. Layout acceptance follows rule 03 (曲箭龙 2026-10-04).
- Contracts decided after dispatch: don't interrupt; record them for integration; resume the same subagent after delivery.
- Do not create `.必要流程说明/`, `改造计划执行/`, or another product's handbooks.

Acceptance — lean:
- Trust no reported number: rerun the scripts. Checks for this repo live under `scripts/`; run the ones that match the change. There is no `tools/qa/run_patrol.ps1` and no `tools/dev/run_admin_tests.ps1`.
- Verify by targeted checks (the implementation, its boundaries, hot spots, and the decided items), not by reading whole diffs.
- Before writing shared data through an API, make sure the local backend runs the latest build; afterwards check structure and flag columns that were not part of the task.
- Reviewers may fix L1 issues and list them; L2+ only report. Systemic problems → whole-batch rework.
- Subtasks report results. 总控 writes 「本轮」 and any ADR update. Subtasks never edit 交接记录, ADR, or 一期未完成事项.
- Ignore intermediate shell-failure notices from running clusters; act on final reports.
- An admin demo does not replace ordinary-role acceptance. Do not fake a payment or drop a hard constraint.
